# The administration's page of AI players (docs/ai-players.md §1, §2, §5):
# the players, a new one, the settings for every AI, the runner tokens.

admin-ai-title = AI players
ai-lead = AI players fill a person's ranked search when nobody else is there, and only for someone who chose to meet one. Each is an account created here: always labelled as an AI, without a password, and played by a runner machine with a runner token. A new one starts switched off.
ai-players = The AI players
ai-none = No AI player yet. Create the first one below.
ai-on = On
ai-off = Off
ai-kind = Kind
ai-kind-hint = It stays as it is once the AI player is created.
ai-profile = Profile
ai-profile-hint = The runner's key for the mind, such as “house:expert”. It stays as it is once the AI player is created, and a profile that sees hidden cards never plays Ranked.
ai-label = Label
ai-label-hint = What every player sees beside its name, such as “Haus-KI · Expert”: 1 to 40 characters.
ai-name = Display name
ai-name-hint = Begins with “KI-”, such as “KI-Haus-Expert”: 4 to 16 characters, ASCII letters and digits with “-” and “_” only between them.
ai-tag = Tag (optional)
ai-tag-hint = Empty to draw one as registration does, or one to eight hex digits.
ai-max-games = Matches at once
ai-max-games-hint = 1 to 16.
ai-daily-games = Games a day
ai-daily-games-hint = Empty for no limit. A language model needs one: 0 to 10,000.
ai-daily-none = No limit
ai-live = Live matches
ai-today = Games today (UTC)
ai-offers = Offers a deck for
ai-offers-none = Nothing
ai-last-sign-in = Runner's last sign-in
ai-never = Never
ai-switch-on = Switch on
ai-switch-off = Switch off
ai-change = Change
ai-remove = Remove
ai-on-title = Switch { $name } on?
ai-on-text = Baylee Central seats it in new matches again, within its own limits and the seats for every AI.
ai-on-done = The AI player is switched on.
ai-off-title = Switch { $name } off?
ai-off-text = It gets no new match from now on, and the matches it plays now end normally. To end those too, revoke its runner token.
ai-off-done = The AI player is switched off.
ai-remove-title = Remove { $name }?
ai-remove-text = Its account goes with everything it holds, its runner's sessions among them. This works only before its first match: after that it stays for good, and you switch it off instead.
ai-removed = The AI player is removed.
ai-played = This AI player has played a match, so it stays for good and keeps its record. Switch it off instead.
ai-edit-title = Change label, limits and name
ai-edit-lead = The kind and the profile stay as they are: a different mind is a different AI player.
ai-save = Save changes
ai-saved = The AI player is changed.
ai-new = New AI player
ai-create = Create AI player
ai-created-done = The AI player is created and switched off. Make a runner token for it, then switch it on.
ai-tag-taken = Another account holds this tag. Choose another one, or leave the field empty to draw one.
ai-invalid-name = The display name must begin with “KI-” and have 4 to 16 characters, ASCII letters and digits with “-” and “_” only between them.
ai-invalid-label = The label needs 1 to 40 characters, without spaces at its ends.
ai-invalid-profile = The profile is a family and a level, such as “house:expert”, in lowercase letters, digits and . _ -, and never one that sees hidden cards.
ai-invalid-games = Matches at once is a number from 1 to 16.
ai-invalid-daily = Games a day is empty or a number from 0 to 10,000, and a language model needs one.
ai-invalid-tag = A tag is one to eight hex digits, such as “#1a2b”, or empty.
ai-settings = Every AI
ai-settings-lead = These limits hold for all AI players together.
ai-settings-changed = Last changed { $time }.
ai-settings-never = Not changed since they were set up.
ai-stopped = Every AI is stopped: there are no AI seats, so no AI gets a new match.
ai-fill-in-after = Wait before an AI fills in (seconds)
ai-fill-in-after-hint = 30 to 600.
ai-drain = Session time a new match needs (minutes)
ai-drain-hint = 30 to 600: a runner's session with less time left gets no new match.
ai-global-seats = AI seats at once
ai-global-seats-hint = 0 to 16. A match between two AIs takes two; 0 stops every AI.
ai-host-reserve = Slots each host keeps for people
ai-host-reserve-hint = 0 to 64.
ai-carousel-games = Matches between two AIs at once
ai-carousel-games-hint = 0 to 8.
ai-carousel-daily = Matches between two AIs a day
ai-carousel-daily-hint = 0 to 10,000.
ai-settings-save = Save settings
ai-settings-saved = The settings for every AI are saved.
ai-settings-invalid = This value is outside its range. Each field says which numbers it takes.
ai-stop-all = Stop every AI
ai-stop-title = Stop every AI?
ai-stop-text = No AI gets a new match from now on: the AI seats go to 0. The matches they play now end normally. To let them play again, set the AI seats above 0.
ai-stop-done = Every AI is stopped.
ai-tokens = Runner tokens
ai-tokens-lead = A runner machine signs in with its token as the AI players the token lists, and as nothing else: no website, no administration, no person's account. Give each machine its own token. Revoking one ends its sessions at once.
ai-tokens-none = No runner token yet.
ai-token-new = New runner token
ai-token-name-hint = The machine that uses it, such as “Runner on bigace”.
ai-token-accounts = The AI players it plays
ai-token-accounts-hint = 1 to 16, fixed for the token's life: to change them, make a new token and revoke this one.
ai-token-no-ai = Create an AI player first: a runner token plays AI players and nothing else.
ai-token-invalid = Give the token a name of up to 64 characters without spaces at its ends, and choose 1 to 16 AI players.
ai-token-shown-lead = The runner sends it to Baylee Central to sign in as the AI players it lists. Keep it only in the runner machine's credential file. Baylee Central keeps only its digest: once you leave this page, nobody can show it again.
ai-token-full = Baylee Central made no token. Either 32 runner tokens are active, or 32 were made in the last day. Revoke one, or try again later.
ai-token-lost = No answer came back, so a token may have been made that nobody can show. Look for it in the list and revoke it.
ai-token-revoke-title = Revoke the runner token “{ $name }”?
ai-token-revoke-text = It stops working at once and ends every session it signed in: the AI players it lists get no new match through it, and the matches they play through it end. This cannot be undone.
ai-token-revoked-done = The runner token is revoked.
